  data: {
    LLM: "Only bid what you think you can make. Count your high cards and consider the talon's potential. In defense, try to force the declarer to use trumps early.\n\nThe talon exchange is crucial - discard cards that don't help your contract. Watch opponents' play to deduce their holdings. Coordinate with the other defender to stop the declarer.\n\nCard counting is essential. Track all trumps and high cards. Bluff in bidding to push opponents into difficult contracts. The Meksiko bid requires perfect hand evaluation.",
